asset:        filmagic-hero.png
title:        README hero: Color workspace, "Apollo 11 - Tranquility" documentary edit
author:       Filmagic contributors (screenshot); footage, transcript and music credits below
source:       original work (screenshot of Filmagic captured with its ui.screenshot control command)
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (screenshot); embedded footage and transcript text are US Government works (public domain), music CC0-1.0
license-file:
added:        2026-11-12 by @vansyson1308
notes:        A 3:12 documentary cut of the Apollo 11 mission, built entirely through Filmagic's control channel
              (docs/images/scripts/build_apollo.py), captured mid-playback in the Color workspace at 2400x1285 points
              (2x, 4800x2570 px) and halved to 2400 px wide (capture_hero.py).
              Shown: Effect Controls of the selected liftoff shot (Motion Scale push-in and Color Grading Exposure
              keyframes, a Basic Correction grade); the Program monitor on the Saturn V's swing arms falling away at
              liftoff from Launch Complex 39A, with a lower-third title (Inter Bold/Regular) and a subtitle from the NASA
              air-to-ground transcript; the Color Grading panel with the shot's Basic Correction; Project bins (list view)
              of NASA selects, mission audio, music and the sequence; a timeline with 49 picture cuts and dissolves on V1,
              B-roll cutaways on V2, five titles on V3, a caption track, nat sound, mission audio and a ducked music bed
              (its ducking keyframes visible), named markers, In/Out around the launch and its rendered preview; live
              loudness meters. All UI icons are drawn in code; fonts are Inter and JetBrains Mono (OFL-1.1). Contains no
              Adobe artwork.
              NASA does not endorse this project. NASA insignia visible inside the 1969 footage are incidental to the
              historical record and are not used as logos.
Media visible or used in the project (none of it is committed to the repository):
  - "Apollo 11 25th Anniversary 'B' Roll Footage" (NASA KSC, NASA ID KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Historical_Footage_and_Broll-DVC_1560;
    1969 NASA film). US Government work, public domain (credited "NASA", no secondary creator).
    Source: https://images.nasa.gov/details/KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Historical_Footage_and_Broll-DVC_1560
  - "Apollo 11 Activities: breakfast, C-7 exit, convoy, white room, hatch closing, launch count and launch" (NASA KSC, NASA ID
    KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Breakfast_C7Exit_Convoy_WhiteRmHatchClosing_Launch-HM_0083; launch-pad camera feeds and
    countdown audio). US Government work, public domain.
    Source: https://images.nasa.gov/details/KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Breakfast_C7Exit_Convoy_WhiteRmHatchClosing_Launch-HM_0083
  - "Apollo 11 Mission Control Center - Film Rolls" (NASA KSC, Launch Control Center Firing Room film, no audio; NASA ID
    KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Mission_Control_Center_Film_Rolls1). US Government work, public domain.
    Source: https://images.nasa.gov/details/KSC-19690716-MH-NAS01-0001-Apollo_11_Mission_Control_Center_Film_Rolls1
  - "Apollo 11 moonwalk montage" (NASA HQ, NASA ID Apollo_11_moonwalk_montage_720p; 1969 lunar-surface TV with
    air-to-ground audio). US Government work, public domain.
    Source: https://images.nasa.gov/details/Apollo_11_moonwalk_montage_720p
  - Subtitle text: "Apollo 11 Technical Air-to-Ground Voice Transcription" (NASA Manned Spacecraft Center, July 1969).
    US Government work, public domain. Source: https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/static/history/alsj/a11/a11transcript_tec.html
    (lines at GET 00 00 00 04, 00 00 00 13, 00 00 01 02, 04 06 38 30, 04 06 45 40, 04 06 45 59, 04 06 46 04, 04 06 46 06,
    04 13 24 48, 04 13 43 16, 04 13 43 24; speakers named from the transcript's CDR/LMP/CC codes, CC as "Houston").
  - Chopin, Nocturne Op. 48 No. 1, performed for Musopen. CC0-1.0. Source: https://archive.org/details/musopen-chopin
    (shown only as a waveform).
Reproduction: docs/images/scripts/README.md lists the downloads and the exact commands. prepare_media.py cuts the
  reels (ffmpeg as a fixture generator only); build_apollo.py builds target/demo-media/Apollo 11 - Tranquility.fcproj
  (bins, imports, 1920x1080 30p sequence, V1 cut with A1 nat sound, V2 cutaways, A2 mission audio with T-0 of the
  countdown on the ignition cut, A3 music, track names, dissolves and audio fades, titles with graphics.newText /
  graphics.set, the caption track from the transcript, Color Grading presets and the hand grade with Scale and
  Exposure keyframes on the liftoff shot, Essential Sound types and generated ducking, markers, In/Out
  00:00:46:15-00:01:34:00 and Render In to Out); capture_hero.py sets up the Color workspace and grabs the window
  0.6 s after playback starts at 00:01:16:27, so the meters are live.
